<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A few representative checks do not prove that every file or setting is correct. If an important item is missing, name it and record the issue rather than accepting a general “everything copied” statement.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="section-2"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Keep the difference between copied and available clear</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For each important example, ask where it is stored and whether its everyday use depends on an account or an unfinished download. You do not need to change a sync setting to ask that question.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If a provider process is still running, record what is expected to continue and who to contact if it does not finish. Do not agree that an unresolved item is complete just because the appointment has ended. Equally, identify separately quoted work rather than assuming an unlimited follow-up is included.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="section-3"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Confirm ownership and recovery</h2>
{% call note("care", "Take care", "Keep ownership and recovery clear") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Make sure you know which account controls the new computer and how you will receive future authentication prompts. Keep recovery information in a place you control. Never put it into a public review, service ticket description or marketing enquiry.</p>{% endcall %}
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Ask what your backup covers after the move. The existence of files on the new computer is not, by itself, an explanation of your backup plan. If backup preparation is outside the agreed move, record that as a separate next step.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="section-4"><span aria-hidden="true">04</span>Keep the old computer until the decision is clear</h2>
{% call note("care", "Take care", "Keep the old computer and original files") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Do not erase or dispose of the old device merely because the new one starts. Retain the original files while you review the agreed result and clarify any exceptions. Erasure and disposal require their own scope and informed decision; this checklist does not provide a wiping procedure.</p>{% endcall %}

<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">The useful outcome is a setup you can use and an honest record of what remains—not a promise that every old setting will be identical.</p>

